<img
src ="img/Polittico_Giotto_card.png">

On your phone the card talks to you “So, the great George sent you to learn precision?" a voice echoes. It’s the Archangel Michael. "Look little guardian, what I learned in fighting with the devil everytime is that the difference between us and him stands in the little things. Draw a card from the level 1 Challenge deck and scan it with your phone to reveal your first challenge. 
[[Draw a challenge card->Challenge_1#]]



:: Box content {"position":"0,775","size":"100,100"}
(set: $box_content to true)
(if: $instructions is false)[

You were right! Inside the box there is a board depicting a sort of blueprint, or maybe a map… oh, wait a second! It’s the Pinacoteca! The place is divided into four distinct zones, each with a dedicated spot where to place the dedicated challenge deck. There’s also a red deck named “artwork”, and… what’s this golden card representing Saint George?

<img src="img/Board.png">

Maybe it’s better to read the instructions to make some sense out of it.

[[Read the instructions ->Instructions]]
]

(if: $instructions is true)[
The box contains a sort of blueprint of the Pinacoteca, where the different level zones are distinguished using different colors, each with its own dedicated spot where to place the dedicated challenge deck. Here it is the artwork deck and the very shiny Saint George card. That’s all! We can start.

<img src="img/Board.png">

[[Download and open the app ->App homepage]]
]


:: Box open {"position":"150,600","size":"100,100"}
You open the box: there isn’t too much stuff inside, at least the game doesn’t seem hard to understand! A board, some decks… You don’t know where to start. Is it better to read the instruction card first or have a look at the box content?

[[Let’s read the instructions ->Instructions]]
[[I want to see what’s inside the box! ->Box content]]


